  "id": "anafranil",
  "term": "Anafranil",
  "definition": "Anafranil is the hydrochloride salt form of clomipramine, a tricyclic antidepressant. It works in the central nervous system by reducing the reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin, which increases the effects of these neurotransmitters, and it also interacts with alpha-adrenergic, histaminergic, and cholinergic receptors.",
